      <h2 id="nw-secondary-ext-gw-configure_configuring-secondary-external-gateway" class="group scroll-mt-20">Configure a secondary external gateway<a href="#nw-secondary-ext-gw-configure_configuring-secondary-external-gateway" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can configure an external gateway on the default network for a namespace in your cluster.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>You installed the OpenShift CLI (<code>oc</code>).</li>
      <li>You are logged in to the cluster with a user with <code>cluster-admin</code> privileges.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>Create a YAML file that contains an <code>AdminPolicyBasedExternalRoute</code> object. For more information, see "AdminPolicyBasedExternalRoute object configuration".</li>
      <li>
      To create an admin policy based external route, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc create -f <file>.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>
      <code>&lt;file&gt;</code>: Specifies the name of the YAML file that you created in a previous step.
      <CodeBlock code={"adminpolicybasedexternalroute.k8s.ovn.org/default-route-policy created"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      <li>
      To confirm that the admin policy based external route was created, enter the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc describe apbexternalroute <name> | tail -n 6"} lang="terminal" />
      <ul>
      <li>
      <code>&lt;name&gt;</code>: Specifies the name of the <code>AdminPolicyBasedExternalRoute</code> object.
      <CodeBlock code={"Status:\n  Last Transition Time:  2023-04-24T15:09:01Z\n  Messages:\n  Configured external gateway IPs: 172.18.0.8\n  Status:  Success\nEvents:  <none>"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      </li>
      </ol>
